Do not remove existing functionality.

Do not introduce unrelated features or change the product's business model.

Only implement the features explicitly specified in this prompt and the previously approved Meridian requirements.

Before coding, inspect the existing project, database, APIs, authentication, integrations and existing demo accounts.

Reuse working components and services.

If a required component already exists, extend it instead of creating a duplicate.

If a necessary change could affect previous phases, make the smallest compatible change and explain it before proceeding.

Do not silently make independent product or design decisions.

## 2. Meridian's Role

Meridian is a SaaS orchestration layer.

It coordinates trade workflows, records agreement information, monitors shipment conditions, analyzes evidence, manages approval workflows and connects with supported third-party services.

It is not a bank, payment processor, escrow agent, shipping provider or legal arbitration authority.

PayPal handles only the payment operations actually supported by its APIs.

The demo uses PayPal Sandbox exclusively.

Never claim that Meridian guarantees delivery, payment, escrow protection or dispute outcomes.

